=== REASONING ===

P1 — Provider port. The handler resolves a provider through the
F1 registry at request time (registry.For(ctx, FeatureID)) BEFORE
opening the SSE response so a provider-resolution error becomes a
JSON 502 rather than a half-opened stream. Strategy code never
imports provider adapters directly — it only consumes the abstract
provider.Provider interface. Mirrors slices 0011-0019.

P4 — Strategy + dispatcher. internal/ai/strategies/rag-help/strategy.go
exports a Strategy struct {FeatureID, System, Tools (read-only F4),
RedactionPolicy (PolicyChatbot), EvalGoldens (loaded at runtime by
F6 harness)}. The handler runs dispatch.New(...denyAllConfirm) which
forbids any tool that requires user confirmation — which is the
chosen mechanism for "no mutations" because retrieve_docs and
cite_help_chunk are both read-only by design (their factories pass
RequiresConfirm=false; the dispatcher's denyAllConfirm gate is the
defense in depth).

P5 — Decorator chain. The handler does not assemble the chain itself;
it consumes the F1 registry-built provider, which in router.go is
already wrapped in the locked decorator order: redact → rate limit
→ cost cap → audit → trace. This is the same wiring path used by
every prior slice (0011-0019).

P6 — Backend guard. The route is mounted via
g.Wrap("rag-help", aiRagHelpHandler) inside mountAIRoutes; the guard
returns 404 in off mode (ADR-015 §I6) before the handler ever runs.

P7 — F4 tools. retrieve_docs and cite_help_chunk are pure read-only
tools registered in internal/ai/tools/help.go. Tools call the F7
retriever (provider.Retriever interface) — they do not create a
duplicate write path. cite_help_chunk converts a chunk reference into
a structured citation envelope; it makes no remote calls.

  Note on the test-only "cite_*" tool prefix exception:
  TestStrategy_ToolsIncludesNoMutators in strategy_test.go uses the
  same allowed read-only prefix list as nl-search, with one addition:
  "cite_*". The slice prompt explicitly names cite_help_chunk as a
  required tool, and the existing whitelist (retrieve_*, hydrate_*,
  query_*, search_*, fetch_*, validate_*, draft_*) does not include
  the citation prefix. The prefix list lives ONLY inside this slice's
  test (it does not leak into other slices' allow-lists). All other
  invariants the test asserts — tool count, defensive copy, RequiresAuth
  per call, RequiresConfirm=false per call — match nl-search exactly.

P8 — Eval. internal/ai/strategies/rag-help/goldens.yaml has 3 goldens
(basic_help, refusal_mutation, zero_matches) plus 3 canned mock-provider
replies under canned/. The F6 harness (cmd/ai-eval -feature rag-help)
exits 0 with 3/3 pass and the all-features run also exits 0 with 33/33
pass.

P9 — Feature registry. internal/ai/features/registry.go gets a new
"rag-help" entry between charging-diagnosis and __redaction_bypass__
with full RouteSet (Backend, Frontend, UITestIDs, JobNames,
PushKinds) and TS mirror regenerated by aigen. The PushKinds slice
is explicitly []string{} (not nil) per the prompt's "If a surface is
truly absent, use []string{} in the implementation instead of
omitting the field" rule.

P10 — Baseline coexistence. The new HelpPage ALWAYS renders the
curated link palette (5 canonical destinations). The AI surface is
selected at composition time by the withAiFeature('rag-help', …)
HOC: if ai_mode='off' OR the rag-help toggle is off, withAiFeature
returns null and the AI section is absent (not greyed-out). The
selection mechanism is therefore a pure HOC at the React render
boundary; no business logic branches on ai_mode anywhere on the
backend or in the page itself.

  Off-mode test:
  TestRagHelpAIOffHidesAssistantAndDocsLinksWork in
  web/src/features/system/__tests__/TestRagHelpAIOffHidesAssistantAndDocsLinksWork.test.tsx
  verifies all five baseline curated links remain visible in off mode
  AND the AI surface root (data-testid=ai-feature-rag-help-root) is
  absent. A positive control case (mode=cloud + toggle on) confirms
  the AI surface DOES appear when both conditions hold.

  Backend-side off-mode test:
  TestRagHelpAIOffHidesAssistantAndDocsLinksWork (Go) probes
  POST /api/v1/ai/help/query through the live mountAIRoutes table and
  asserts a 404 in off mode AND that a non-AI baseline /help endpoint
  remains 200. The two halves of the same-named test together prove
  the §I3+§I5+§I6 invariants for this slice.

App.tsx + routeRegistry.ts non-touch rationale:
  The slice prompt's allowed-files block does NOT include App.tsx or
  web/src/lib/routeRegistry.ts. Two slice precedents (digest-narration,
  yir-narration, nl-alert-builder) likewise registered a Frontend
  route in metadata without wiring it through App.tsx — instead the
  AI surface ships inside an existing baseline page, and the new
  HelpPage's import path is exercised by the Vitest off-mode test
  through MemoryRouter. The registry's Frontend route ("/help") is
  metadata for the final-gate Playwright walk; the actual SPA mount
  point can be added in a follow-up commit if the final gate flags
  the missing route. This keeps the slice within the explicit
  allowed-files boundary (no scope drift, ADR-015 §I3 honored).

Redaction policy:
  PolicyChatbot from internal/ai/redact/policies.go. App docs and i18n
  keys contain no user PII, so the Allow set is empty; redaction is
  symmetric (input + output) with no round-trip required. The strategy
  test asserts strategy.RedactionPolicy is exactly PolicyChatbot and
  has empty Allow.

Background job:
  ai_docs_indexer is registered in the registry's JobNames per the
  prompt. The implementation is a fail-closed gate stub: it reads
  settings.ai_mode + the rag-help toggle and returns immediately if
  AI is off OR the feature is disabled. Real indexing of docs/runbooks/
  i18n is out of scope for this slice; future work will populate the
  embeddings table the F7 retriever queries. Until then, retrieve_docs
  returns zero matches against runbooks/i18n source types. The
  goldens use canned mock-provider responses so deterministic eval
  works without real index data.

